{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he flew.</b> When the ע״י [root letters] have a kamatz and it is read with a ḥataf, it is from the root עוף; and when it has a pataḥ it is from the root עיף." "<b>Ritzpah.</b> A coal, like עוגת רצפים." "And the sense of <b>with tongs</b> is in the manner of a human being." "And the sense of <b>the altar</b> is because the fire is pure, not foreign."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:26.568458309Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}